IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- MAINTENANCE OF CHILDREN AND ATTENDANCE AT SCHOOL
-- (regulations 65 to 67).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 645 to 663.
--
-- Regulation 65: when a survivor maintains the contributor's dependent children "wholly or substantially" (more than half).
-- Regulation 65.1: what "maintaining the child" means. Regulation 66: full-time and part-time attendance at a school or
-- university, and when an absence (a vacation, an illness) is counted as attendance. Regulation 67: the attestation
-- filed for a child aged 18 or more. Section 2(2) of the Act is not applied to "18 or more years of age" in regulation 67,
-- which speaks of a state and not of "reaching" an age (fork F-67).

§ `Part V -- Maintenance of children and attendance at school (regulations 65 to 67)`

§§ `Regulation 65 -- wholly or substantially`

-- src:646 | 65 For the purposes of subsection 42(1) of the Act, wholly or substantially, with reference to the maintenance of one or more dependent children of a deceased contributor, means that the survivor of that contributor provides more than 50 per cent of the maintenance provided for such children by all persons other than such children or any other dependent child of that contributor.
@ref Reg 65 (src:646)
GIVEN `the maintenance the survivor provides for the dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `the maintenance provided for the dependent children by all persons other than the children and any other dependent child of the contributor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 65 — the survivor maintains the dependent children wholly or substantially`
    `the maintenance the survivor provides for the dependent children`
    `the maintenance provided for the dependent children by all persons other than the children and any other dependent child of the contributor` MEANS
    `the maintenance the survivor provides for the dependent children` GREATER THAN
        (`the maintenance provided for the dependent children by all persons other than the children and any other dependent child of the contributor` TIMES 0.5)

§§ `Regulation 65.1 -- maintaining the child`

-- src:649 | 65.1 For the purposes of subsection 42(1) and paragraph 76(1)(d) of the Act, maintaining the child
-- src:650 | (a) with reference to the child of a deceased contributor, means making periodically, for the child, until the contributor’s death, financial provision amounting to not less than the orphan’s benefit payable under the Act; and
-- src:651 | (b) with reference to the child of a disabled contributor, means making periodically, for the child, financial provision amounting to not less than the disabled contributor’s child’s benefit payable under the Act.
@ref Reg 65.1(a) (src:650)
GIVEN `the person made financial provision for the child periodically until the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the periodic financial provision` IS A NUMBER
      `the orphan's benefit payable under the Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 44(1)(f) and the section that fixes its amount (pieces cp3 and cp4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 65.1(a) — a person maintains the child of a deceased contributor`
    `the person made financial provision for the child periodically until the contributor's death`
    `the periodic financial provision`
    `the orphan's benefit payable under the Act` MEANS
    `the person made financial provision for the child periodically until the contributor's death`
        AND `the periodic financial provision` AT LEAST `the orphan's benefit payable under the Act`

@ref Reg 65.1(b) (src:651)
GIVEN `the person made financial provision for the child periodically` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the periodic financial provision` IS A NUMBER
      `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 44(1)(e) and the section that fixes its amount (pieces cp3 and cp4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 65.1(b) — a person maintains the child of a disabled contributor`
    `the person made financial provision for the child periodically`
    `the periodic financial provision`
    `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act` MEANS
    `the person made financial provision for the child periodically`
        AND `the periodic financial provision` AT LEAST `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act`

§§ `Regulation 66 -- attendance at a school or university`

-- src:654 | 66 (1) For the purposes of paragraph (b) of the definition dependent child in subsection 42(1) of the Act,
-- src:655 | (a) full-time attendance at a school or university, with respect to a child, means that the child attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature and is enrolled in courses that constitute a course load recognized by the educational institution as full-time study; and
-- src:656 | (b) part-time attendance at a school or university, with respect to a child, means that the child, without being in full-time attendance at a school or university, attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature and is enrolled in courses that constitute at least 20 per cent of a course load recognized by the educational institution as constituting a full course load.
@ref Reg 66(1) (src:654-656)
GIVEN `the child attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is enrolled in courses that constitute a course load recognized by the institution as full-time study` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share of a full course load recognized by the institution that the child's courses constitute` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cr2 Attendance at a school or university`
`reg 66(1) — the attendance of a child at a school or university`
    `the child attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature`
    `the child is enrolled in courses that constitute a course load recognized by the institution as full-time study`
    `the share of a full course load recognized by the institution that the child's courses constitute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the child attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature`)
           THEN `no attendance at a school or university`
        IF `the child is enrolled in courses that constitute a course load recognized by the institution as full-time study`
           THEN `full-time attendance at a school or university`
        IF `the share of a full course load recognized by the institution that the child's courses constitute` AT LEAST 0.2
           THEN `part-time attendance at a school or university`
        OTHERWISE `no attendance at a school or university`

-- 66(2): a child who would be in attendance but is absent during a normal period of scholastic vacation is considered in attendance.
-- src:657 | (2) A child referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) who is absent from the educational institution during any normal period of scholastic vacation is considered to be in full-time or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution during that period.
@ref Reg 66(2) (src:657)
GIVEN `the attendance the child has apart from the absence` IS A `cr2 Attendance at a school or university`
      reason IS A `cr2 Reason a child is absent from the educational institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 66(2) — the child is considered to be in attendance during a normal period of scholastic vacation`
    `the attendance the child has apart from the absence` reason MEANS
    (NOT (`the attendance the child has apart from the absence` EQUALS `no attendance at a school or university`))
        AND reason EQUALS `the child is absent during a normal period of scholastic vacation`

-- 66(3): absent because of illness: in attendance during the absence if the child resumes immediately after, in the same
-- academic year, or (where the Minister has determined the child unable to) in the following academic year.
-- src:658 | (3) A child referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) who is absent from the educational institution because of illness is, during the period of that absence, considered to be in full-time attendance or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution if
-- src:659 | (a) immediately after that absence and during the same academic year, the child resumes full-time or part-time attendance at any educational institution; or
-- src:660 | (b) in the case where the Minister has determined that the child is unable to comply with paragraph (a), the child resumes full-time or part-time attendance at any educational institution in the following academic year.
@ref Reg 66(3) (src:658-660)
GIVEN `the attendance the child has apart from the absence` IS A `cr2 Attendance at a school or university`
      reason IS A `cr2 Reason a child is absent from the educational institution`
      `the child resumes attendance at any educational institution immediately after the absence and during the same academic year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has determined that the child is unable to resume attendance in the same academic year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child resumes attendance at any educational institution in the following academic year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 66(3) — the child absent because of illness is considered to be in attendance during the absence`
    `the attendance the child has apart from the absence`
    reason
    `the child resumes attendance at any educational institution immediately after the absence and during the same academic year`
    `the Minister has determined that the child is unable to resume attendance in the same academic year`
    `the child resumes attendance at any educational institution in the following academic year` MEANS
    (NOT (`the attendance the child has apart from the absence` EQUALS `no attendance at a school or university`))
        AND reason EQUALS `the child is absent because of illness`
        AND (    `the child resumes attendance at any educational institution immediately after the absence and during the same academic year`
              OR (    `the Minister has determined that the child is unable to resume attendance in the same academic year`
                  AND `the child resumes attendance at any educational institution in the following academic year`))

-- src:661 | (4) A child referred to in paragraph (3)(b) is considered to be in full-time attendance or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution until the end of the normal period of scholastic vacation that follows the academic year in respect of which the child was determined by the Minister to be unable to resume attendance.
@ref Reg 66(4) (src:661)
GIVEN `the child is a child referred to in paragraph (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the normal period of scholastic vacation that follows the academic year in respect of which the child was determined unable to resume attendance` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 66(4) — the child is considered to be in attendance on a day`
    `the child is a child referred to in paragraph (3)(b)`
    `the end of the normal period of scholastic vacation that follows the academic year in respect of which the child was determined unable to resume attendance`
    day MEANS
    `the child is a child referred to in paragraph (3)(b)`
        AND day AT MOST `the end of the normal period of scholastic vacation that follows the academic year in respect of which the child was determined unable to resume attendance`

-- src:662 | (5) A child referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) who is absent from the educational institution because of illness and who, during this absence, dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor’s child is considered to have been in full-time or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution until the end of the month in which they die or in which they cease to be a dependent child or disabled contributor’s child.
@ref Reg 66(5) (src:662)
GIVEN `the child is absent because of illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death or of ceasing to be such a child` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 66(5) — the last day the child is considered to have been in attendance`
    `the child is absent because of illness`
    `the child dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child during the absence`
    `the date of the death or of ceasing to be such a child` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `the date of the death or of ceasing to be such a child` PLUS (0 MINUS 1)

@ref Reg 66(5) (src:662)
GIVEN `the child is absent because of illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death or of ceasing to be such a child` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 66(5) — the child is considered to have been in attendance on a day`
    `the child is absent because of illness`
    `the child dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child during the absence`
    `the date of the death or of ceasing to be such a child`
    day MEANS
    `the child is absent because of illness`
        AND `the child dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child during the absence`
        AND day AT MOST
            (`reg 66(5) — the last day the child is considered to have been in attendance`
                `the child is absent because of illness`
                `the child dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child during the absence`
                `the date of the death or of ceasing to be such a child`)

§§ `Regulation 67 -- the attestation for a child aged 18 or more`

-- src:663 | 67 An applicant or beneficiary who claims that a dependent child of 18 or more years of age is or was for a period in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university shall file with the Minister an attestation to that effect, signed by the child, and any supporting documentation.
@ref Reg 67 (src:663)
GIVEN `the applicant or beneficiary claims that a dependent child is or was for a period in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dependent child is 18 or more years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 67 — the applicant or beneficiary must file an attestation signed by the child and supporting documentation`
    `the applicant or beneficiary claims that a dependent child is or was for a period in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university`
    `the dependent child is 18 or more years of age` MEANS
    `the applicant or beneficiary claims that a dependent child is or was for a period in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university`
        AND `the dependent child is 18 or more years of age`

@ref Reg 67 (src:663)
GIVEN `an attestation signed by the child is filed with the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `supporting documentation is filed with the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 67 — what is filed meets the regulation`
    `an attestation signed by the child is filed with the Minister`
    `supporting documentation is filed with the Minister` MEANS
    `an attestation signed by the child is filed with the Minister` AND `supporting documentation is filed with the Minister`
